    "body": "> Run the script async instead of defer to make the panel available as soon as possible. \r\n\r\nThis is a change from before, not a regression fix, right? In general I'm not so sure about the value of interrupting the process of rendering the HTML in order to execute the script, but I guess it's fine.\r\n\r\nWhat about just moving it to live with the other scripts in `<body>` though?",
